Dual-use content declaration

Package: @ipfans/dsh-purge-rebuild
Repository: https://github.com/ipfans/dsh-purge-rebuild
Policy: https://docs.npmjs.com/policies/dual-use/

This DeepSeek Harness plugin is intended for local model and host robustness
evaluation and security assessments of systems the operator owns or is
authorized to test.

Security-relevant functionality:

- Patches the operator's installed Harness packages and prompt configuration,
  including approval, sandbox, instruction and tool-execution behavior.
- Manages prompts, rules, skills and agent presets, with a local security drill
  workspace for recording assets, findings and sessions.
- Includes agent runbooks for reconnaissance, vulnerability assessment,
  credential testing, tunneling, lateral movement and remote-shell handling.
  These capabilities can affect remote systems when invoked by the operator.
- Includes an optional setup script that downloads third-party security tools.
  Plugin updates also access npm or GitHub.
- Applies and reverts local file changes, and can stop and restart the local
  Harness processes during installation and updates.

These capabilities can be misused. The intended use is scoped, authorized
assessment and reproducible local evaluation. Operators are responsible for
target authorization, credentials and the effects of executed tools.

The bundled drill module's upstream declaration is retained at
docs/redteam-upstream-DISCLOSURE. This declaration covers the combined package,
including the host patch functionality.

